---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Term from "../components/Term.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
const GH = "https://github.com/wookat/witness";
---
<Base title="Witness Docs — install, record, hand evidence to your agent">
<section style="padding:120px 0 40px"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">Docs</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:10px">Everything after the landing page.</h2>
  <p class="lede">What Witness is, what it installs, how to configure it, how to record — and exactly what your agent receives.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:18px;font:500 12.5px var(--mono);color:var(--faint)">
    <a href="#what">01 what</a> · <a href="#install2">02 install</a> · <a href="#config">03 configure</a> · <a href="#use">04 use</a> · <a href="#output">05 the package</a> · <a href="#agent">06 tell your agent</a> · <a href="#try">07 try it</a>
  </p>
</div></section>

<div class="ruler"><b class="a">docs</b><i style="--x:4%"></i></div>

<section id="what"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">01 · What it is</div>
  <h2 class="rv">A black box for product QA.</h2>
  <p class="lede rv" data-d="60">Witness records a human using a web product and turns it into <b>causal evidence</b> an AI coding agent can act on. You talk and point; it keeps the books. One continuous take can hold many issues — segmentation is optional.</p>
  <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:34px">
    <Card icon="mic" n="VOICE" title="Continuous speech" d="0">Live streaming ASR (Doubao web → IME → browser SR fallback, all free). Every spoken observation lands on the timeline verbatim — corrections never overwrite the original.</Card>
    <Card icon="zap" n="OPS" title="Causal bursts" d="60">Each click captures its ~1.8s aftermath: requests, response bodies, console errors, DOM mutations. A click with <b>no</b> aftermath is recorded as evidence of a dead button.</Card>
    <Card icon="layers" n="STATE" title="Page forensics" d="120">rrweb full replay, event-driven screenshots, DOM snapshots, element marks with React/Vue component chains. No source-line mapping needed — selectors + components are enough.</Card>
  </div>
  <p class="lede rv" data-d="140" style="margin-top:26px">Stopping produces a local evidence package under <code>.witness/sessions/&lt;timestamp&gt;/</code> — nothing leaves your machine unless you hand it to an agent.</p>
</div></section>

<div class="ruler"><b class="a">install</b><i style="--x:18%"></i></div>

<section id="install2" class="alt"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">02 · Install</div>
  <h2 class="rv">One package, no downloads, no keys.</h2>
  <p class="lede rv" data-d="60">Witness is a CLI (<code>wit</code>), not a browser extension. It drives your <b>system Edge or Chrome</b> through Playwright — no browser download, no cloud account.</p>
  <Term label="terminal" d="80"><span class="c-dim"># requires Node 18+ · Windows/macOS/Linux · system Edge/Chrome</span>
npm i -g github:wookat/witness
wit --version                     <span class="c-dim"># verify</span>
wit start http://localhost:5173   <span class="c-dim"># first recording</span></Term>
  <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:30px">
    <Card icon="box" title="What gets installed" d="0"><b>the <code>wit</code> CLI</b> — recorder, session renderer, transcriber, MCP server. Global config at <code>~/.witness/config.json</code>, ASR credentials cached at <code>~/.witness/doubao-creds.json</code>. Evidence always lands in the <b>current project's</b> <code>.witness/sessions/</code>.</Card>
    <Card icon="terminal" title="Or let your agent install it" d="60">Paste this to any coding agent — it can install, verify and record for you:<pre style="margin-top:10px;font:12px/1.7 var(--mono);background:var(--warm);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px;white-space:pre-wrap">Install witness: `npm i -g github:wookat/witness`,
verify with `wit --version`, then run
`wit start http://localhost:5173` and tell me
when the managed browser opens.</pre></Card>
  </div>
</div></section>

<div class="ruler"><b class="a">config</b><i style="--x:36%"></i></div>

<section id="config"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">03 · Configure</div>
  <h2 class="rv">Zero-config by default; switches when you want them.</h2>
  <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:34px">
    <Card icon="mic" title="Live ASR engine" d="0"><code>wit config asr</code> persists to <code>~/.witness/config.json</code>; <code>--asr</code> / <code>WIT_ASR</code> override per run. Agents can flip it live via the <code>set_asr</code> MCP tool.<pre style="margin-top:10px;font:12px/1.8 var(--mono)">auto         doubao-web → doubao-ime → sr
doubao-web   best punctuation (default pick)
doubao-ime   per-sentence timestamps, ITN digits
sr           browser SpeechRecognition (offline)
off          no live subtitles (final transcript only)</pre></Card>
    <Card icon="shield" title="Optional keys &amp; env" d="60">Everything works with none of these — they're upgrades, not requirements:<pre style="margin-top:10px;font:12px/1.8 var(--mono)">OPENAI_API_KEY   whisper-1 word timestamps
ZHIPU_API_KEY    GLM-4 say-correction + associate
WIT_ASR          engine override for one run
WIT_NO_BODIES=1  skip response-body capture
WIT_CDP=&lt;port&gt;   expose CDP so an agent can drive
                 the recorded browser as the tester</pre></Card>
  </div>
</div></section>

<div class="ruler"><b class="a">record</b><b class="b">● REC</b><i style="--x:52%"></i></div>

<section id="use" class="alt"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">04 · Use it</div>
  <h2 class="rv">Talk, point, keep going.</h2>
  <p class="lede rv" data-d="60">Run <code>wit start &lt;url&gt;</code> from your project root. A managed browser opens — use the product normally and <b>say what you see out loud</b>. Live subtitles appear under the toolbar.</p>
  <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:30px">
    <Card icon="eye" title="While recording" d="0"><pre style="font:12.5px/2 var(--mono)">Ctrl+Click   mark an element (selector + shot + DOM)
M            inspect mode — hover-pick or drag a region
N            split a new issue boundary (optional)
P            pause/resume — freezes evidence AND mic
Alt+Shift+R  stop · or the ■ button · or Ctrl+C</pre></Card>
    <Card icon="file" title="After stopping" d="60"><pre style="font:12.5px/2 var(--mono)">wit list                 all sessions
wit open                 latest review.html
wit transcribe &lt;dir&gt;     re-run transcription
wit correct &lt;dir&gt;        LLM polish (verbatim kept)
wit associate &lt;dir&gt;      LLM picks evidence per SAY
wit recover &lt;dir&gt;        rebuild after a crash
wit mcp [dir]            serve evidence over MCP</pre></Card>
  </div>
</div></section>

<div class="ruler"><b class="a">package</b><i style="--x:70%"></i></div>

<section id="output"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">05 · What you get</div>
  <h2 class="rv">One package, two audiences.</h2>
  <p class="lede rv" data-d="60"><b>For you:</b> a visual replay. <b>For your agent:</b> a structured handoff it can fix from.</p>
  <Term label=".witness/sessions/&lt;ts&gt;/" d="80">├─ <span class="c-acc">review.html</span>      <span class="c-dim">→ FOR HUMANS — timeline replay: audio + shots + events, click anything to seek</span>
├─ <span class="c-ok">PROMPT.md</span>        <span class="c-dim">→ FOR AGENTS — handoff doc: how to read this evidence</span>
├─ <span class="c-ok">session.md</span>       <span class="c-dim">→ FOR AGENTS — the timeline: every SAY + its causal burst</span>
├─ events.jsonl     <span class="c-dim">→ raw event stream (1189 events in a real run)</span>
├─ transcript.json  <span class="c-dim">→ final speech transcript, segment timestamps</span>
├─ audio.webm       <span class="c-dim">→ the recording, seekable</span>
├─ shots/           <span class="c-dim">→ screenshots — marks get red boxes, regions are crops</span>
├─ bodies/          <span class="c-dim">→ request/response payloads</span>
├─ dom/             <span class="c-dim">→ DOM snapshots at key moments</span>
├─ rrweb.jsonl      <span class="c-dim">→ full replay stream</span>
└─ session.json     <span class="c-dim">→ meta: url, duration, asr engine, counts</span></Term>
  <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:30px">
    <Card icon="file" title="PROMPT.md" d="0">The paste-this-to-your-agent doc. Teaches it the format: causal-burst indentation, "no aftermath = evidence", component chains, never infer intent without a SAY.</Card>
    <Card icon="clock" title="session.md" d="40">The evidence timeline. Each <code>SAY</code> block carries your verbatim words plus what the page did at that second.</Card>
    <Card icon="api" title="wit mcp" d="80">Serves the session over stdio MCP: <code>session_overview</code> · <code>list_says</code> · <code>session_md</code> · <code>events_around</code> · <code>get_errors</code> · <code>get_shot</code> · <code>get_dom_state</code> · <code>get_body</code> · <code>get_asr</code> · <code>set_asr</code>.</Card>
  </div>
</div></section>

<div class="ruler"><b class="a">handoff</b><i style="--x:86%"></i></div>

<section id="agent" class="alt"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">06 · Tell your agent</div>
  <h2 class="rv">Three ways to hand over evidence.</h2>
  <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:34px">
    <Card icon="terminal" n="EASIEST" title="Point at the directory" d="0"><pre style="font:12px/1.8 var(--mono)">"I recorded a session —
evidence is in .witness/sessions/&lt;ts&gt;.
Read session.md and fix the issues."</pre></Card>
    <Card icon="file" n="FOR ANY AGENT" title="Paste PROMPT.md" d="40">The file teaches an unfamiliar agent how to read the package. Copy its contents plus the directory path — works with agents that don't know Witness.</Card>
    <Card icon="api" n="PERMANENT" title="Wire the MCP" d="80"><pre style="font:12px/1.8 var(--mono)">&#123; "mcpServers": &#123; "witness": &#123;
  "command": "wit", "args": ["mcp"]
&#125; &#125; &#125;</pre>Agent pulls evidence on demand — and can flip the ASR engine itself.</Card>
  </div>
  <p class="lede rv" data-d="120" style="margin-top:26px">And to make an agent <b>record</b>: <code>"use witness to record http://localhost:5173 — I'll talk through the issues"</code>. With <code>WIT_CDP</code> set, an agent can even <b>be the tester</b> inside the recorded browser.</p>
</div></section>

<div class="ruler"><b class="a">demo</b><b class="b">■ STOP</b><i style="--x:96%"></i></div>

<section id="try"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">07 · Try it in two minutes</div>
  <h2 class="rv">Record the demo page.</h2>
  <p class="lede rv" data-d="60">A tiny broken product ships with the site — it has a dead button, a console error and a bad API response waiting to be caught:</p>
  <Term label="terminal" d="80">wit start https://witness.zalize.com/demo-app.html --duration 60
<span class="c-dim"># click the Pay button, say "点了没反应", stop → open review.html</span></Term>
  <div class="cta rv" data-d="140" style="display:flex;gap:12px;margin-top:30px">
    <a class="btn pri" href="/demo-app.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the demo app ↗</a>
    <a class="btn" href={GH}>GitHub ★</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/">← Back to landing</a>
  </div>
</div></section>
</Base>
